//? Title: Match Rating name comparison
//? Subtitle: Actual codex byte decisions, aligned cancellation and heuristic limits
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Comparing name spellings requires a rule for compressing letters and judging
their remaining differences. The native Match Rating Approach produces bounded
codexes, cancels aligned letters from both ends and compares an integer
similarity with a length-dependent threshold. We expose actual producing
decisions, retain the original twelve name pairs, and show why heuristic
acceptance is neither proof of identity nor a transitive equivalence relation.
)

\toc

> Specify the native codex rules

Process the original bytes in order. Ignore spaces and nonalphabetic bytes under
the active C locale, uppercase alphabetic bytes, keep the first letter, then
keep a consonant only if it differs from the preceding alphabetic source letter.
Even an omitted vowel updates that previous-letter state. The retained
implementation therefore encodes Babab as BBB: it does not run a separate
duplicate-collapse pass after deleting vowels. This detail matters when
comparing MRA variants.

If the kept stream has at most six letters, return it; otherwise concatenate its
first three and last three. The native analysis exposes actual normalized
letters, actual kept stream and final codex from that one loop. These are
byte-oriented ctype operations, not UTF-8 accent normalization or a
language-independent pronunciation model. The examples use ASCII letters under
the normal C locale.

> A tiny actual filter and trim

Ashcraft produces normalized ASHCRAFT, kept stream ASHCRFT and final codex
ASHRFT. The table reads each actual raw-byte decision, including previous-letter
state and the real kept-stream length before/after that byte. The diagram reads
actual phase strings.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/match_rating_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/match_rating.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t = dm::algorithms::match_rating_codex_trace("Ashcraft");
    std::print("| actual raw index | raw byte | actual uppercase byte | previous alphabetic byte | kept | " "kept length before | kept length after |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- | ---: | ---: " "|\n");
    for (auto &s : t.steps)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", s.index,
                   unsigned(s.raw), unsigned(s.upper), unsigned(s.previous),
                   s.kept, s.before, s.after);
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("normal", {0, 0},
           std::format("Actual normalized letters\n{}", t.analysis.normalized)).node("kept", {6, 0}, std::format("Actual kept stream\n{}", t.analysis.stripped)).node("trim", {12, 0}, std::format("Actual bounded codex\n{}", t.analysis.codex)).edge("normal", "kept").edge("kept", "trim");
    d.save_svg("build/match_rating_tiny.svg");
}
```
