> Derive the pair score and retain the original examples

Let the two final codex lengths be l1,l2. If their absolute difference is at
least three, return not comparable with no cancellation pass. Otherwise the
minimum is5 for combined length up to4,4 up to7,3 up to11 and2 for12. The native
convention includes combined length zero in the first case.

Align the codexes from the left. Equal positions cancel; unequal existing
letters append to each side’s residual. Align those residuals from the right,
cancel equal positions and count remaining unequal existing letters u1,u2. The
similarity is6−max(u1,u2); acceptance requires it to reach the selected minimum.
Missing letters are absent positions, not alphabetic zero bytes. Swapping inputs
swaps residuals/counts while preserving threshold and maximum, proving symmetry.

The original twelve pairs are mechanism fixtures without ground-truth person
labels. Their plotted similarities are not estimates of identity probability or
measured classification accuracy. Not-comparable pairs are shown in the table
but omitted from the score plot.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/match_rating_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/match_rating.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto pairs = dm::algorithms::match_rating_demo_pairs();
    std::vector<double> x, score, threshold;
    std::print("| original pair index | first name | second name | actual first codex | actual second codex " "| comparable | similarity | minimum | heuristic match |\n| ---: | --- | --- | --- | --- | " "--- | ---: | ---: | --- |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < pairs.size(); ++i) {
        auto a =
            dm::algorithms::match_rating_analyze(pairs[i].first, pairs[i].second);
        auto &r = a.result;
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", i,
                   pairs[i].first, pairs[i].second, a.codex_a, a.codex_b,
                   r.comparable, r.similarity, r.min_rating, r.match);
        if (r.comparable) {
            x.push_back(i);
            score.push_back(r.similarity);
            threshold.push_back(r.min_rating);
        }
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.points(x, score, "actual similarity");
    p.line(x, threshold, "actual threshold", {220, 38, 38});
    p.y_limits(0, 7).x_label("original pair index in table order").y_label(
        "actual integer score or selected threshold").title(
        "Original name pairs: actual heuristic scores").save_svg(
        "build/match_rating_original.svg");
}
```
