> Inspect the real two-pass cancellation

Byrne versus Boern exposes why reverse alignment matters. The original codexes
differ in length, so unequal left-aligned residuals can still share
right-aligned suffix letters. The native trace records every actual compared
pair, equality decision and count transition. Byte values are printed as
unsigned integers to keep absent zero and literal letters unambiguous in MEP
output.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/match_rating_cancellation.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/match_rating.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t = dm::algorithms::match_rating_trace("Byrne", "Boern");
    std::print("Actual codexes `{}` and `{}`; actual forward residuals `{}` and `{}`.\n\n| actual reverse " "pass | offset from active end | first byte0 if absent | second byte0 if absent | equal | " "first count before | first count after | second count before | second count after |\n| --- " "| ---: | ---: | ---: | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n",
               t.analysis.codex_a, t.analysis.codex_b, t.analysis.residual_a,
               t.analysis.residual_b);
    std::vector<double> x, a, b;
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < t.cancellations.size(); ++i) {
        auto &s = t.cancellations[i];
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",
                   s.reverse, s.index, unsigned(s.a), unsigned(s.b), s.equal,
                   s.before_a, s.after_a, s.before_b, s.after_b);
        x.push_back(i);
        a.push_back(s.after_a);
        b.push_back(s.after_b);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(x, a, "first side count");
    p.line(x, b, "second side count", {22, 163, 74});
    p.x_label("actual cancellation record index").y_label(
        "residual length, then unmatched count").title("Actual forward and reverse cancellation phases").save_svg("build/match_rating_cancellation.svg");
}
```
